---
import { withBase } from "../lib/url";
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="About Surfer Element | Tamraght, Morocco"
  description="Surfer Element is a booking service in Tamraght, Morocco, representing three independent surf houses. Here's exactly how we work and who pays us."
  navLabel="About"
>
  <section class="container section prose">
    <h1>About Surfer Element</h1>
    <p>Surfer Element is a booking service based in Tamraght, Morocco. We
      work with three independent surf houses, SurfsHUB Tamraght, Cactus
      Surf &amp; Skate House and Hakuna Matata Guest House, and help
      travellers book a stay at whichever one fits them, in their own
      language, with a single deposit.</p>
    <p>We are not a surf house ourselves, and we don't run the surf program
      at any of the three. Each house is independently owned and run; we
      handle the comparison, the booking, the payment, and being on the
      ground in Tamraght to help if something comes up during your stay.</p>

    <h2>Who pays us</h2>
    <p>We're upfront about this: Surfer Element is paid by the three houses
      listed on this site, and we represent only them. We don't claim to be
      an independent directory of every surf camp in Tamraght. There are
      more than twenty, and we only work with three. What we do promise is
      that the information we show about each one &mdash; the scores, the
      guest-review themes, the "good fit if / not a fit if" lines &mdash;
      comes from real, dated, sourced data, not from what a house would
      prefer we say about it.</p>

    <h2>How we chose these three houses</h2>
    <p>All three are in Tamraght itself (not neighbouring Taghazout, which
      some listings confuse it with), run the same surf program at the same
      price, and have real, checkable guest-review histories on Booking.com.
      What differs between them is the day-to-day feel of each house, which
      is exactly what <a href={withBase("/compare/")}>the comparison page</a> and
      <a href={withBase("/fit-check/")}>the fit check</a> are for.</p>

    <h2>What we actually do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Compare the houses honestly</strong>, using real
        Booking.com scores and paraphrased guest-review themes, dated and
        linked to the source, never our own marketing description.</li>
      <li><strong>Take a 15% deposit on this site</strong> when you book, so
        you don't have to juggle three different booking processes.</li>
      <li><strong>Keep your price locked in</strong> once you book, even if
        that house's own direct price rises afterward.
        <a href={withBase("/price-lock/")}>How the price lock works &rarr;</a></li>
      <li><strong>Have a real, in-person presence in Tamraght</strong>, not a
        booking platform based somewhere else. We greet guests and help
        arrange transfers, including the airport pickup that's included in
        every package.</li>
      <li><strong>No fixed office hours.</strong> Airport pickups happen
        whenever a flight lands, so instead of posting opening hours, we're
        reachable by <a href={withBase("/contact/")}>contact</a> whenever you need us.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="pending">Our exact street address is pending and not yet published here or anywhere else on the site.</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <div class="photo-gallery" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr; max-width: 20rem;">
      <div class="photo-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 4/5;">Team photo coming soon</div>
    </div>
    <p class="pending">A short, honest line about who's behind Surfer Element is pending — nothing is invented here.</p>

    <h2>Languages</h2>
    <p>This site is published in English, German, French, Spanish, Italian
      and Dutch. Our own team communicates with guests in English or French.
      Some house staff speak additional languages; see each house's profile
      page for what's actually confirmed, rather than assuming.</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p><a href={withBase("/faq/")}>Read the FAQ &rarr;</a> or <a href={withBase("/contact/")}>get in touch &rarr;</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
